# The archive itself is the product: elections/ is committed, always.
#
# Two things must never be committed, and both are here on purpose:
#   * raw source downloads — election.toml records the URL, retrieval date and SHA-256,
#     which is what makes a bundle reproducible. Keeping the multi-megabyte original is
#     not the archive's job. The cache lives in ~/.cache/wahlwerk-data/, outside the
#     repo; the data/ rule below only catches a download aimed here by hand.
#   * anything derived — a bundle is rebuilt with `uv run wahlwerk-ingest`, never
#     patched into shape and committed.
#
# And two are committed deliberately, so they are absent from this file:
#   * uv.lock       — pinned dev toolchain; ingest output must be reproducible.
#   * .python-version — the interpreter the bundles were built with.
#
# Note the absence of a *.gz rule: tally.csv.gz is a bundle file, not an artefact.

# Raw source dumps, if fetched into the repo rather than the cache
data/
*.csv.orig

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.env
.envrc

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.cache/
.tox/
.nox/

# Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.cover

# Type checkers
.pyre/
.pytype/

# Editors and IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code local overrides (.claude/settings.json is shared and committed)
.claude/settings.local.json
